# The fuzz/regression corpus (proptest directoryBasedDatabase, slice 5) is strict
# binary — [u8 version][u64 counts][raw serialized choice bytes]. With
# core.autocrlf=true (this repo's setting) git's content heuristic could rewrite
# embedded 0x0A → 0x0D 0x0A on add/checkout, silently corrupting the replay data.
# `-text` alone only suppresses CRLF normalization; git's diff/merge machinery
# still falls back to its own binary-sniffing heuristic per file, which a small
# corpus entry (a version byte + a handful of choice bytes, not guaranteed to
# contain a NUL in the first chunk) can slip past. Use git's built-in `binary`
# macro (`-diff -merge -text`) so corpus entries are never normalized, diffed, or
# 3-way-merged — a merge conflict on a corpus file should hard-stop, not silently
# splice two byte streams together.
tests/corpus/** binary
